RepoLaunch
=====================================================================
swe-brew follows the agent-prompt structure and the ``result.json`` manifest
field conventions of RepoLaunch
(https://github.com/microsoft/RepoLaunch), which is licensed under the MIT
License, so that RepoLaunch-compatible tooling can consume swe-brew output
and so that the agent's setup/organize loop is familiar to RepoLaunch users.
See:
  src/swe_brew/agent/prompt.py        (setup/organize system prompt structure)
  src/swe_brew/benchmark/result_json.py   (result.json field conventions)

